  "paper_reference": {
    "paper_question": "参数只能定到一个集合时，识别集合如何写成准则函数的零集，估计量与置信区域如何由样本准则函数的等值集构造？",
    "target": "项目自建有限模型中的六门店链式全政策均值：六家门店全部接入共享库存时，等权平均达标率的识别集合。",
    "source_location": "Section 2 (pp. 1246-1247) for Theta_I = {theta in Theta : Q(theta) = 0}, the moment-inequality set {theta : E_P[m_i(theta)] <= 0} in (2.1), and the statement that with linear moment functions Theta_I is an intersection of linear half-spaces; p. 1248 Example 1 for interval data with Theta_I = {theta : E[Y1] <= theta <= E[Y2]}; p. 1250 and p. 1253 for the contour set C_n(c). The numeric [7/12, 3/4] is NOT from this paper.",
    "formula": "参照组：链式相邻网络 门店1—门店2—门店3—门店4—门店5—门店6，同伴暴露=严格过半邻居接入，平票为0。原试点每轮均匀固定抽 2 个名额；目标政策为全接入（每家自身处理=1），此时每家门店的暴露都是1，目标格子统一为（自身=1、暴露=1）。两类约束：门店1、门店6 的该格子是等式约束（试点揭示 3/4）；门店2-5 的该格子是双边夹逼约束（档案 [1/2, 3/4]，且该格子需要 3 个名额、试点只有 2 个，在分配律下概率为零，故只能落在界限里）。目标 theta = 六个格子均值的等权平均，识别集合下界 4*(1/2)/6 + 2*(3/4)/6 = 1/3 + 1/4 = 7/12；上界 4*(3/4)/6 + 2*(3/4)/6 = 1/2 + 1/4 = 3/4；宽度 1/6。与论文写法对应：六个格子给出六条约束，Theta_I 是这些约束在半空间交里截出的线段，下界绑在四条档案下界加两条等式、上界绑在四条档案上界加两条等式。变化版只评门店2-5（纯夹逼、没有等式）：识别集合退化为档案区间本身 [1/2, 3/4]，宽度 1/4，正是论文例 1 的 [E Y1, E Y2] 在本题的逐字形态。",
    "conditions": [
      "Complete finite mean model: only the listed exact population signature means and the archive bounds are known.",
      "No full joint distribution and no extra aggregate means are provided.",
      "Each store's mean lies in [1/2, 3/4] under every complete binary assignment (archive record).",
      "Mean sufficiency: each store's potential-outcome mean depends only on own treatment and strict-majority peer exposure, for all binary assignments.",
      "Known assignment law: uniform fixed quota of 2 out of 6.",
      "Consistency, randomization independence, fixed pre-treatment network, finite first moments.",
      "No additional cross-unit or cross-context coupling constraints."
    ],
    "sharpness_argument": "The two endpoint cells are equalities at 3/4, contributing 2*(3/4)/6 = 1/4. Each of the four interior cells is independently free within [1/2, 3/4], contributing [4*(1/2)/6, 4*(3/4)/6] = [1/3, 1/2]. Lower endpoint 1/3 + 1/4 = 7/12 and upper endpoint 1/2 + 1/4 = 3/4 are both attainable, so the interval is sharp relative to the declared finite mean model; the engine certificate reports sharp=true.",
    "what_paper_supports": [
      "The identified set as the zero set of a nonnegative population criterion, Theta_I = {theta : Q(theta) = 0}, generally multivalued (p. 1246).",
      "Moment-inequality characterization (2.1) and the statement that with linear moment functions Theta_I is an intersection of linear half-spaces (p. 1246).",
      "Moment-equality characterization (2.4)-(2.6) with the GMM criterion (p. 1247).",
      "Example 1: interval data with Theta_I = {theta : E[Y1] <= theta <= E[Y2]} and a two-kink criterion (p. 1248).",
      "Contour sets of the sample criterion as the general form of estimates and regions (p. 1250; equation (3.2) on p. 1253)."
    ],
    "what_paper_does_not_support": [
      "It does not supply the numeric [7/12, 3/4] or [1/2, 3/4].",
      "It does not supply the six-store chain network, the quota design, the archive bounds, or the known/bracketed split.",
      "Its estimation and inference machinery (the choice of c-hat, subsampling on p. 1257, asymptotics of C_n on p. 1259, Hausdorff rates and the degeneracy property on pp. 1251 and 1254) has no counterpart in this deterministic finite model.",
      "It does not claim that Theta_I as defined is sharp; sharpness here is a property of the declared finite model, checked by replaying the certificate, not a citation."
    ]
  },
